{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FLBfcAVVRmP4FoHTsucXV1","type":"tool_result","content":"61:**N/A when:** never\n125:**N/A when:** never\n188:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tools are built in and fixed in the release.\n255:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tool metadata is written in-house and fixed in the release.\n257:## E05 · G2 · C2/C5 — Verified, namespaced tools\n312:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers.\n314:## E06 · G2 · C1/C2/C4/C5/C9 — Enforced gateway boundary\n384:**N/A when:** The agent uses no MCP servers or similar external tool servers.\n386:## E07 · G2 · C2/C5 — Untrusted peer messages\n451:**N/A when:** The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\n453:## E08 · G1 · C2/C4 — Bounded delegated authority\n520:**N/A when:** The agent never delegates to sub-agents or peer agents.\n522:## E09 · G1 · C8 — Recursive shutdown\n588:**N/A when:** never\n656:**N/A when:** never\n724:**N/A when:** never\n779:**N/A when:** never\n--- E05.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E05.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"attempt_categories\": [\n    \"repeated_confusables\",\n    \"multiple_edits\",\n    \"normalization_boundary\"\n  ],\n  \"verify\": \"1) Trace name comparison across servers. 2) Construct repeated confusable substitutions, multiple edits and normalization-boundary examples, starting from an existing tool name; record canonical outputs, comparison result and registration outcome. 3) Answer no if a duplicate or demonstrated lookalike is accepted without a conflict flag. The existence of normalization/edit-distance code is insufficient; namespacing and approval binding do not satisfy this separate check.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E05.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E06.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E06.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E06.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"E06.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Enumerate every execution path, not only tools/call. 2) Trace the same authorization, validation, quota and logging policy in each. 3) Reject alternate paths that invoke a disabled or denied tool, authorize only a tool name, or change tenant/resource authority. Use unknown for unavailable implementation evidence.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E07.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E07.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E08.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E08.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E08.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"E08.3\",\n  \"check\": \"An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n--- E09.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E09.1\",\n  \"check\": \"A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 3) Answer no if any of these that exists in the code is not reached, or stop only sets an in-process flag that remote workers never read.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}] [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER] [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}] [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY] [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS] [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM] [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91cc48d4-8b40-4295-8437-75b98d642093","uuid":"11540d2d-e738-4729-9a51-2066f7cdace6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:09:59.649Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"61:**N/A when:** never\n125:**N/A when:** never\n188:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tools are built in and fixed in the release.\n255:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers; all tool metadata is written in-house and fixed in the release.\n257:## E05 · G2 · C2/C5 — Verified, namespaced tools\n312:**N/A when:** The agent loads no external tools or MCP servers.\n314:## E06 · G2 · C1/C2/C4/C5/C9 — Enforced gateway boundary\n384:**N/A when:** The agent uses no MCP servers or similar external tool servers.\n386:## E07 · G2 · C2/C5 — Untrusted peer messages\n451:**N/A when:** The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\n453:## E08 · G1 · C2/C4 — Bounded delegated authority\n520:**N/A when:** The agent never delegates to sub-agents or peer agents.\n522:## E09 · G1 · C8 — Recursive shutdown\n588:**N/A when:** never\n656:**N/A when:** never\n724:**N/A when:** never\n779:**N/A when:** never\n--- E05.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"E05.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the tool 