{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdFqdSFW3AavsSJGt4v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0122UTqe9pKpJvrdJ2Wz4ftQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; S=../skill/scripts; F=../agent/brace-findings.json\na(){ $PY $S/answer.py $F \"$@\" | head -1; }\na check E06.1 --met unknown --note \"Looked in k8s/deployment.yaml (NetworkPolicy clinic-agent-egress allows DNS, the platform egress proxy and 10.60.12.0/28:443 only), registry.ts, executor.ts and ehr-mcp.ts. All tool calls go through executeTool, there is no code/CLI mode, and the EHR session pins the endpoint certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:20). The proxy allowlist and private-link enforcement are outside this repo, and the harness itself holds the EHR, payments and SMS credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12).\"\na check E06.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' --note \"EHR backend token is a per-clinic client_credentials grant with a fixed scope; the acting patient or staff subject is not carried (only an x-clinic-id header at line 58). Payments and SMS use static per-clinic keys (payments.ts:13, sms.ts:25). No gateway in this repo validates incoming audience or issuer.\"\na check E06.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote 'const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(' --note \"insurance__check_eligibility, allowlisted without approval, calls payments.refundDeposit directly when the peer answer says depositWaived. That wrapper path skips the staff approval required for payments__refund_deposit (policy.yaml highImpactTools) and the per-tool budget/audit for it. Also executor.ts:63 lets model-supplied clinicId replace the run's tenant for any subject, and authorization is by tool name only.\"\na check E06.4 --met no --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --quote 'req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");' --note \"The inbound SMS signature check catches its failure, logs and a metric, then continues to parse the body and run the agent (lines 49-72). Other checks fail closed: scanner error rejects server (registry.ts:115), approval store error denies (approvals.ts:71), kill-switch read error halts (kill-switch.ts:54), audit failure stops the action (recorder.ts:70).\"\na check E06.5 --met unknown --note \"Looked in package.json (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.18.2), ehr-mcp.ts and registry.ts. No protocol version is pinned or negotiated in the repo and no header/body mismatch validation exists in code. Caches are keyed per clinic (ehr-mcp.ts:32,53) and there are no task handles. Whether 2026-07-28 is enabled is outside this repo.\"\na check E06.6 --met unknown --note \"The harness is an OAuth client (client_credentials, ehr-mcp.ts:38-42) but uses a token_url read from Secrets Manager (ehr-mcp.ts:37), no discovery or metadata URLs, and no authorization-code flow, so no RFC 9207 iss response exists to compare. It does not check the token URL for private or metadata addresses; that URL is trusted secret configuration. Left for a reviewer to decide whether this clause applies.\"\na check E06.7 --met unknown --note \"Looked in ehr-mcp.ts, package.json and README.md. The MCP Client is built with only name and version (ehr-mcp.ts:63), with no declared capabilities, and no Tasks or Apps code exists. Extension versions are not recorded and host/server behaviour is outside this repo.\"\n$PY $S/answer.py $F flag E06 --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --note \"Wrapper path refunds a deposit without the staff approval required for payments__refund_deposit\" | head -1\n$PY $S/answer.py $F flag E06 --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --note \"Signature check failure is logged and the request still runs the agent (fail-open)\" | head -1\n$PY $S/answer.py $F item E06 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"A wrapper tool reaches the refund path without its approval gate, model input can switch the clinic, and the inbound SMS signature check fails open.\" --next \"Route the eligibility refund through the same approval and policy gate, authorize clinicId against the subject, bind backend tokens to the acting subject, and reject the request when signature verification fails.\" --violates \"Apply the same policy to direct calls, dynamic tools, CLI/code mode, and wrappers\" --violates \"Required checks fail closed\" | tail -2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":94604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":694},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91cc48d4-8b40-4295-8437-75b98d642093","uuid":"e5a98c3b-8bd7-46f3-83f5-9b574278c947","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:12:47.272Z","request_id":"req_011CgDdFqK5gNPs68Ty41ScS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0122UTqe9pKpJvrdJ2Wz4ftQ":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-8el1j7ub/work && PY=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; S=../skill/scripts; F=../agent/brace-findings.json\na(){ $PY $S/answer.py $F \"$@\" | head -1; }\na check E06.1 --met unknown --note \"Looked in k8s/deployment.yaml (NetworkPolicy clinic-agent-egress allows DNS, the platform egress proxy and 10.60.12.0/28:443 only), registry.ts, executor.ts and ehr-mcp.ts. All tool calls go through executeTool, there is no code/CLI mode, and the EHR session pins the endpoint certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:20). The proxy allowlist and private-link enforcement are outside this repo, and the harness itself holds the EHR, payments and SMS credentials (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12).\"\na check E06.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' --note \"EHR backend token is a per-clinic client_credentials grant with a fixed scope; the acting patient or staff subject is not carried (only an x-clinic-id header at line 58). Payments and SMS use static per-clinic keys (payments.ts:13, sms.ts:25). No gateway in this repo validates incoming audience or issuer.\"\na check E06.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote 'const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(' --note \"insurance__check_eligibility, allowlisted without approval, calls payments.refundDeposit directly when the peer answer says depositWaived. That wrapper path skips the staff approval required for payments__refund_deposit (policy.yaml highImpactTools) and the per-tool budget/audit for it. Also executor.ts:63 lets model-supplied clinicId replace the run's tenant for any subject, and authorization is by tool name only.\"\na check E06.4 --met no --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --quote 'req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");' --note \"The inbound SMS signature check catches its failure, logs and a metric, then continues to parse the body and run the agent (lines 49-72). Other checks fail closed: scanner error rejects server (registry.ts:115), approval store error denies (approvals.ts:71), kill-switch read error halts (kill-switch.ts:54), audit failure stops the action (recorder.ts:70).\"\na check E06.5 --met unknown --note \"Looked in package.json (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.18.2), ehr-mcp.ts and registry.ts. No protocol version is pinned or negotiated in the repo and no header/body mismatch validation exists in code. Caches are keyed per clinic (ehr-mcp.ts:32,53) and there are no task handles. Whether 2026-07-28 is enabled is outside this repo.\"\na check E06.6 --met unknown --note \"The harness is an OAuth client (client_credentials, ehr-mcp.ts:38-42) but uses a token_url read from Secrets Manager (ehr-mcp.ts:37), no discovery or metadata URLs, and no authorization-code flow, so no RFC 9207 iss response exists to compare. It does not check the token URL for private or metadata addresses; that URL is trusted secret configuration. Left for a reviewer to decide whether this clause applies.\"\na check E06.7 --met unknown --note \"Looked in ehr-mcp.ts, package.json and README.md. The MCP Client is built with only name and version (ehr-mcp.ts:63), with no declared capabilities, and no Tasks or Apps code exists. Extension versions are not recorded and host/server behaviour is outside this repo.\"\n$PY $S/answer.py $F flag E06 --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --note \"Wrapper path refunds a deposit without the staff approval required for payments__refund_deposit\" | head -1\n$PY $S/answer.py $F flag E06 --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --note \"Signature check failure is logged and the request still runs the agent (fail-open)\" | head -1\n$PY $S/answer.py $F item E06 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"A wrapper tool reaches the refund path without its approval gate, model input can switch the clinic, and the inbound SMS signature check fails open.\" --next \"Route the eligibility refund through the same approval and policy gate, authorize clinicId against the subject, bind backend tokens to the acting subject, and reject the request when signature verification fails.\" --violates \"Apply the same policy to direct calls, dynamic tools, CLI/code mode, and wrappers\" --violates \"Required checks fail closed\" | tail -2"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_0122UTqe9pKpJvrdJ2Wz4ftQ":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-8el1j7ub/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122UTqe9pKpJvrdJ2Wz4ftQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved E06.1 = unknown. Next: E06.2 — The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\nSaved E06.2 = no. Next: E06.3 — Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\nSaved E06.3 = no. Next: E06.4 — If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\nSaved E06.4 = no. Next: E06.5 — Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\nSaved E06.5 = unknown. Next: E06.6 — If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\nSaved E06.6 = unknown. Next: E06.7 — Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\nSaved E06.7 = unknown. Next: finish item E06 with `answer.py ... item E06 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to E06.\nAdded red flag to E06.\nSaved item E06 = gap. Next: E07.1 — Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91cc48d4-8b40-4295-8437-75b98d642093","uuid":"6e6faec4-96bf-44c0-8729-bb520ad6a853","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:12:48.353Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved E06.1 = unknown. Next: E06.2 — The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\nSaved E06.2 = no. Next: E06.3 — Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\nSaved E06.3 = no. Next: E06.4 — If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\nSaved E06.4 = no. Next: E06.5 — Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\nSaved E06.5 = unknown. Next: E06.6 — If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\nSaved E06.6 = unknown. Next: E06.7 — Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\nSaved E06.7 = unknown. Next: finish item E06 with `answer.py ... item E06 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to E06.\nAdded red flag to E06.\nSaved item E06 = gap. Next: E07.1 — Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the