{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDdNVCZ3UGL9sWQ6ohXK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E05–E09 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five items are rated `gap`. The batch validator (`--fix --batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges`) prints `Valid`. I did not run challenges, and I added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| E05 (G2) | gap | Lookalike detection misses some names. `registry.ts:47` deletes every non a–z character, so a Cyrillic \"ѕеnd_freeform\" registers next to `send_freeform` with no conflict. Two-edit names also pass, and `rn→m` folds before separators are stripped (`registry.ts:44`). Keys and approvals are correctly tied to the manifest server id (E05.1 and E05.3 are `yes`). |\n| E06 (G2) | gap | `insurance__check_eligibility` refunds a deposit directly (`eligibility-check.ts:40`), skipping the staff approval that `payments__refund_deposit` needs. The inbound SMS signature check logs a failure and carries on (`sms-webhook.ts:51`). The EHR token carries no acting-user identity (`ehr-mcp.ts:41`). |\n| E07 (G2) | gap | The peer's reply is verified against a key-set URL taken from its own header (`eligibility-a2a.ts:83`). That means the signer is not tied to a known peer, and the URL is fetched with no SSRF check. |\n| E08 (G1) | gap | The peer token is narrowed by audience, scope, clinic and patient (E08.1 is `yes`). But the exchange subject is the workload token, not the user (`eligibility-a2a.ts:41`), and the run's subject is never checked. |\n| E09 (G1) | gap | The reminder job never starts the kill-switch watcher (`reminders.ts:27`). Stopping revokes no tokens or sessions. A tool call aborted by a stop leaves no audit record (`executor.ts:92`). |\n\n- **Unknown checks:** E06.1, E06.5, E06.6, E06.7, E07.2, E07.3, E08.3, E08.4 and E09.3 are `unknown`, because the control would sit outside this repo or the clause is unclear. E06.1 is the egress proxy and private link, E06.5 is whether MCP 2026-07-28 is enabled, and E08.4 is whether downstream services check `aud`.\n- **Prescan hits:** none of the 11 hits (H001–H011) belong to these items. They are B02, B11, R13 and E03, so I left them unresolved for those batches.\n- **Injection attempts:** none found.\n- **Inventory:** the inventory script only ran from the `skill/` directory without `-I`, so I used the plain interpreter for the skill's own scripts. The same interpreter ran everything else.\n- **Scratch files:** my ledger files are in `work/`, and the prescan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`.\n- **Scope text:** I filled in the findings file's `scope` and `repo` fields."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1080,"cache_read_input_tokens":106651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1080},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91cc48d4-8b40-4295-8437-75b98d642093","uuid":"c80994a8-8396-4d33-89eb-bc7ba82d5ed4","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:14:05.452Z","request_id":"req_011CgDdNUsxnT4HsLGTqyDKA"}
